<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="68ab3bf6"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="3eb428fd">&lt;p&gt;
    A test script is the implementation of a test case. For automated testing, test scripts are commonly written in
    computer programming languages. The test case defines how functionality is validated; a test script contains
    the instructions to validate that the functionality behaves as expected. For manual testing, a test script
    contains textual step-by-step instructions to perform what is specified in the test case.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
